From: Clifford Swartz <cliffordswartz1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:01:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] hw/adc: AVR8X 12-bit differential ADC (AVR64EA48)

Conversions completed at once on COMMAND.START (IMMEDIATE, MUXPOS/MUXNEG
write; free-running every 20 us of virtual time): single 12-bit, 8-bit,
series and burst accumulation of up to 1024 samples (with scaling),
differential (signed, +-VREF over +-2048), LEFTADJ, SAMPLE, the window
comparator, RESRDY/SAMPRDY cleared by reading RESULT/SAMPLE, overrun
flags, three vectors (ERROR, RESRDY, SAMPRDY). Inputs: AIN0-31 from the
board ("ain", as the ARM ADC models), GND, VDD/10, the temperature
sensor (its code from "temperature" through SIGROW.TEMPSENSE0/1, the
data sheet's formula inverted). References VDD, VREFA, 1.024, 2.048,
2.5, 4.096 V. New overlay; regenerated tables.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted; not for submission to upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
